      "category": "Text",
      "text": "a. The New York City Mayor's Office of Housing Recovery Operations (HRO) shall continue to coordinate with the New York City Health and Hospitals Corporation (H+H) and other agencies as appropriate, to operate temporary humanitarian relief centers to be known as \"Humanitarian Emergency Response and Relief Centers\" (\"HERRCs\") to provide assistance to asylum seekers, by offering respite, food, medical care, case work services, and assistance in accessing a range of settlement options, including through connections to family and friends inside and outside of New York City, in addition to, if needed, direct referrals to alternative emergency supports.",
